---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is an independent reimplementation of the science sandboxes
framework. The framework itself, the specimens/assays/oracle structure, the
wet/damp/dry distinction, and the idea of an invented genetic world come from:

  Rao, A. S., Castro, R. I., Gosai, S. J., Hsu, K. B., Ektefaie, Y.,
  Singh, S., Bhatia, S. N., Reilly, S. K., Tewhey, R., Lander, E. S.,
  and Sabeti, P. C. "Science sandboxes measure the scientific capability
  of AI agents." arXiv:2608.30165 [q-bio.QM], 2026.

Their own implementation is at https://github.com/asr2210/science-sandbox and
is released under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Arya Rao. This project
matches that license as a courtesy. No code was copied from it; the ideas were
reimplemented from the paper.

Note for anyone building a damp sandbox here: their README states that the
Malinois model weights are subject to the separate boda2 license. Any sandbox
that uses those weights inherits that condition, and MIT does not cover it.
